# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# The replay viewer is a route the client owns, not a file on disk, so Pages
# has to be told to serve the app for it (doc 08 phase 7.2, repo CLAUDE.md
# section 3: "Replay served under /replay").
#
# Only `/replay` is routed, deliberately, and not `/replay/*`. The build uses
# `base: "./"` so one bundle works from a project root and from a preview
# deployment's sub-path, which means asset references are relative and resolve
# against the current URL's directory. `/replay` has directory `/` and loads
# the same assets the game does; `/replay/abc-123` has directory `/replay/`
# and would ask for `/replay/assets/index-*.js`, which does not exist. Routing
# that shape here would turn a 404 into a blank page, which is worse. The
# canonical link is `/replay?id=...` and it is what the viewer hands out.
/replay  /index.html  200
